language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Cards 1 to n are arranged in a circle; the frog starts on card 1 and from card k jumps k places clockwise, and must land on every card.
given n : int(1..)
$ x[i] is the card at position i of the circle, with card 1 at position 1
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
$ visit[k] is the position the frog lands on at its k-th stop
find visit : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)

branching on [x]
such that
$ the cards are the numbers 1 to n, each once
allDiff(x),
$ the frog starts on card 1, which is at position 1
x[1] = 1,
$ the frog starts at position 1
visit[1] = 1,
$ the frog lands on a different card at each of the n stops, so it visits every card
allDiff(visit),
$ from card k at a position the frog jumps k places clockwise round the circle
forAll k : int(1..n-1) . (visit[k+1] = ((visit[k] - 1 + x[visit[k]]) % n) + 1)
